# THESIS WORK -- NOT FOR PUBLICATION.
# t1/sdevice_fefet_idvg.cmd and .par are adopted verbatim from the user's own
# GAA-FeFET thesis calibration (autocal/cal_template.cmd, par_template.par).
# They encode his pulsed-write / sub-coercive-read protocol and his fitted
# material parameters -- the results of his calibration work, and unpublished.
# The repository is PUBLIC. These files must never be committed.
t1/sdevice_fefet_idvg.cmd
t1/sdevice_fefet_idvg.par
t1/*.par
t1/*.cmd
t1/calibration.local.json

# Credentials. The repo is PUBLIC and .env holds the Sentaurus password, so this
# rule is load-bearing, not hygiene. .env.example is the committed template.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Sentaurus scratch (never commit vendor binaries or Synopsys-shipped decks)
t1_scratch/
*.tdr
*.plt.gz
_remote_tmp/

# Figures are regenerated; the replay cache is NOT ignored.
results/figures/
!results/cache/
!results/cache/**

# results/runs/ is ignored EXCEPT for the evidence. G10 asks to show the
# per-iteration backend+hash log and D6 attaches it to the writeup, so an ignored
# provenance.jsonl is an ignored answer to the one question the project exists to
# answer. Same for the per-run step logs: the trust-region ratios in them ARE V5.
# These are small append-only text files; the bulk (plots, .tdr, .plt) is what
# the exclusion is for.
#
# Note the shape. Excluding the DIRECTORY (`results/runs/`) makes the "!" lines
# below dead letters -- git does not descend into an excluded directory, so a
# file inside one cannot be re-included. Exclude the contents instead.
results/runs/*
!results/runs/provenance.jsonl
# EVERY top-level measurement JSON, not a hand-maintained list.
#
# CHANGED 2026-08-29 (D6). The list used to name the D3 files one by one, with a
# comment saying "without these the writeup cites files that are not in the
# repository". The comment was right and the list was never extended: by D6,
# ELEVEN artefacts that D4, D5, D6 and the README cite by name -- the H-ablation,
# the budget sweep, the FoM correlations, the corrected V6 control, the manifold
# cloud, the container smoke test, the Tier C replay, the provenance audit and
# both figure banks -- were sitting untracked while the documents pointed at
# them. A rule nobody remembers to extend is a rule that fails quietly.
#
# So: all of them, by shape rather than by name. These are the outputs of the
# measurement scripts in scripts/ -- 21 files, 396 KiB in total -- and the bulk
# this exclusion exists for (plots, .tdr, .plt, per-probe dumps) is not JSON at
# the top level of results/runs/.
!results/runs/*.json
!results/runs/*/
results/runs/*/*
!results/runs/*/steps.jsonl
!results/runs/*/result.json

# The mock cache is regenerated in seconds and is keyed on the mock's own source,
# so committing it buys nothing. Tier C is about results/cache/sentaurus/.
results/cache/mock/

# The MIT-BIH .npz is a rebuild of the thesis' own preprocessing of a public
# database. It is 16 MB, it is not this project's to publish, and it is
# regenerated from DIFFSILICON_ECG_DIR in about eight seconds. See
# src/diffsilicon/snn/ecg.py.
results/cache/ecg/

# `tesseract-runtime serve` drops a run_<uuid>/ beside the working directory for
# every request it handles. They hold logs, nothing reproducible.
run_*/

# The url backend writes what came off a wire into its own directory, stamped
# with the URL rather than a solver name. Nothing reads it back -- the url path
# does not consult a cache, by design, so that a Tier B call is always a real
# call -- and a directory of entries nothing references would read as orphans in
# the provenance audit.
results/cache/url/
